## 7. What to Avoid

1. **Gym / bro clichés** — flexing silhouettes, six-pack torsos, sweaty hero shots, chalk, "no pain no gain." This article's stance is _intelligence over grind_; the visual must read as an instrument, not a hype poster.
2. **A sprawling flowchart.** The source is a decision tree; rendering it literally makes a tangle of arrows. The compact 3×3 matrix _is_ the upgrade — keep it a lookup grid.
3. **Clever-but-empty labels.** Cell names must diagnose in plain language. If a label needs the article to be understood, it has failed (this is the specific flaw to fix from the first draft).